 rigin-y: 50%\; --block-transform: none\; opacity: var(--opacity\, 1)\; tra
 nsform: var(--block-transform)\; transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--o
 rigin-y)\; } Join multiple Archibald Portrait Prize finalist David Fenogli
 o for a two-day portrait painting workshop. The workshop will focus on nat
 ural and realistic representation of the live model in oils. Limited to 8 
 places. 9am - 3:30pm both days. An alla prima approach will be demonstrate
 d\, including blocking in shapes\, proportion\, anatomy\, design\, value/c
 olour relationships\, colour mixing and paint handling. Foundational princ
 iples will be discussed while demonstrating a variety of technical approac
 hes. Day one will focus on anatomy and proportion with students creating a
  block-in drawing and one short alla prima painting from the live model. D
 ay two will focus on modelling form\, colour mixing and paint application 
 with students creating one longer alla prima painting from a live model. #
