BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-16o7gql@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260928T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260928T200000
SUMMARY:Sukundimi Walks Before Me
DESCRIPTION:Q&A Panel screening. New Farm Cinemas: Mon 28 September. Q&A wi
 th Manu Peni. The Sepik River is the mother line for Papua New Guinea comm
 unities. Winding through mountains and rainforests\, she is the crucial ve
 rtebrae connecting and supporting the region’s rare biodiversity and spi
 ritual consciousness. But her livelihood and her communities are threatene
 d by the proposal of a copper-gold mine being built near her waters\, whic
 h could extract\, erode and pollute an environment that she has sustained 
 for millennia. The children of this river\, led by Manu Peni\, create a gr
 assroots campaign to stop the mine from being built\, resisting the forces
  of colonial bureaucracy and Western narratives of ‘development’ by in
 voking the Spirit of the river and indigenous knowledge. Sukundimi Walks B
 efore Me explores this existential fight through lyrical expressions of ex
 istence\, resistance and life along the mother river.
LOCATION:New Farm Cinemas\, 701 Brunswick St\, New Farm
URL:https://www.fivestarcinemas.com.au/new-farm/movie/sukundimi-walks-befor
 e-me
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-zzo626@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260928T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260928T220000
SUMMARY:Botanic By Night: NightGlow
DESCRIPTION:Botanic By Night: NightGlow makes its Brisbane debut at Brisban
 e Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha from 25 September to 10 October\, transformi
 ng the Gardens into a magical after-dark outdoor art experience. Visitors 
 will journey along an enchanting 800-metre route featuring 11 larger-than-
 life illuminated animal sculptures inspired by Queensland's native wildlif
 e. Designed by Ample Projects in collaboration with First Nations artists 
 Casey Coolwell-Fisher and Nathan Peckham\, Botanic By Night: NightGlow com
 bines art\, storytelling and sound to celebrate the animals\, habitats and
  stories that shape Queensland's natural environment. From kangaroos and k
 oalas to platypus\, dingoes and green tree frogs\, each artwork offers a u
 nique encounter\, inviting visitors to wander\, explore and connect with n
 ature in a whole new way. Perfect for families\, friends and date nights\,
  Botanic By Night: NightGlow also features a dedicated food truck precinct
 .
LOCATION:Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha\, Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt
  Coot-tha\, 152 Mt Coot-tha Road\, Toowong
URL:https://botanicbynight.com.au/
END:VEVENT
