BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-me10jf@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T073000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T083000
SUMMARY:Mindful Art Mornings
DESCRIPTION:Start your day with intention at Museum of Brisbane. Mindful Ar
 t Morning invites early risers to the Museum before opening hours for a ge
 ntle\, guided moment of pause. Within the calm of the gallery\, this rotat
 ing program offers an artist-led mindful experience designed to help you r
 eset\, reconnect and ease into the day ahead. After the session\, linger o
 ver a light morning tea\, with space for quiet conversation and reflection
 . MoB is more than a museum - it is a place for the people\, a portal to o
 ur past\, and a mirror to contemporary life. Make Mindful Art Mornings you
 r restorative midweek ritual in the heart of the city. For individual sess
 ion details\, please visit the MoB website. Presented by Museum of Brisban
 e in association with Brisbane Festival. Museum of Brisbane is Brisbane Ci
 ty Council’s leading history and art museum\, where you can experience o
 ur city’s vibrant culture.
LOCATION:Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane City\, Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane
  City Hall\, 64 Adelaide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://museumofbrisbane.t.qtix.com.au/events/019eaeb1-4087-f11b-0c69-c
 da5244fec29
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-199nw5p@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T120000
SUMMARY:Wetlands weaving workshop (15+ years)
DESCRIPTION:Join a cosy morning of weaving at this small group experience f
 or ages 15+ years with contemporary fibre artist Monique Ross. Take some t
 ime out for yourself\, relax\, and connect creatively with nature while le
 arning weaving skills using raffia palm fibre. Suitable for beginners\, al
 l materials supplied. This workshop will take place indoors. About the art
 ist: Monique teaches from a contemporary craft perspective aligned with na
 ture connection and mindfulness. Monique is not an Indigenous artist and d
 oes not teach or represent Indigenous cultural practices. This activity is
  for the general public. If you are a daycare or vacation group interested
  in attending a similar activity\, send an email . Requirements: Arrive 10
  minutes early to register with staff. Hat\, sun-smart clothing\, enclosed
  shoes. Bring a cushion to sit on the carpet if you would like to use one.
  Bring sunscreen and insect repellent. Please BYO water and snacks as ther
 e are no food outlets on site. Note: Events are subject to weather and env
 ironmental conditions and may be cancelled on the day. *Image: Supplied co
 urtesy Heartwood Nature Bathing.
