BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1c36caa@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260916T120000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T160000
SUMMARY:Geoffrey Burns: Ride the Chronovore
DESCRIPTION:Revisiting locations at different times of year\, Geoffrey Burn
 s approaches making as both a method and a measure of time. Works emerge t
 hrough repeated encounters with place\, where observation accumulates and 
 memory takes form through surface and seasonal change. Ride the Chronovore
  considers time as an active force: consuming\, transforming and leaving i
 ts evidence behind. Through repetition\, Burns traces how surfaces shift\,
  forms appear and recede\, and environments register cycles that often unf
 old beyond human attention. Each return gathers new information while reve
 aling what has altered\, disappeared or endured. The fleeting span of a hu
 man life meets the slower tempo of the natural world\, inviting an attenti
 ve and materially grounded way of looking at the quiet force of time. Open
 ing Night Friday September 18 6 - 8pm VIP Preview from 5.30pm Geoffrey Bur
 ns in Conversation Sunday September 20 3pm - 4pm + celebratory drinks with
  the artist until 5pm Artist in Residence Saturday September 26 12pm - 4pm
  (drop in any time) Morning Musings Workshop Retreat Sunday October 4 10am
  - 12pm
LOCATION:PARKER Contemporary\, 38 Hope Street
URL:https://www.parkercontemporary.com.au/exhibitions/geoffrey-burns
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1hk6798@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261220
SUMMARY:Priya Gore art display
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy the latest display by Brisbane artist Priya Gore\, at Boo
 ndall Wetlands Environment Centre as part of the Community Art Wall. Priya
  Gore is a Brisbane-based artist. She finds that " …Australian rainfores
 ts offer the abundance of natural wonder. The bush walks and coastal hikes
  replenish the emptiness of the soul with a long-lasting creative energy. 
 " The artist's life revolves around the exploration of nature’s intricac
 ies that are often hidden in the obvious. This ongoing display can be view
 ed from September to December: Tuesday to Friday\, 9am-4pm Saturday and Su
 nday\, 9am-12pm. About the Community Art Wall: Located in the Boondall Wet
 lands Environment Centre\, the Community Art Wall is a small\, ongoing dis
 play which aims to celebrate and promote environmental awareness through a
 rt by featuring work from local artists and community groups that reflect 
 environmental themes such as sustainability\, biodiversity and connection 
 to nature. If you are interested in displaying your art on the Community A
 rt Wall\, please see opportunities for artists .
LOCATION:Boondall Wetlands Environment Centre\, Boondall Wetlands Environme
 nt Centre\, 31 Paperbark Drive (entry via Stanworth Rd)\, Boondall
URL:https://www.brisbane.qld.gov.au/libraries-venues-and-facilities/venue-a
