BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-384zm7@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260927T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260927T220000
SUMMARY:Botanic By Night: NightGlow
DESCRIPTION:Botanic By Night: NightGlow makes its Brisbane debut at Brisban
 e Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha from 25 September to 10 October\, transformi
 ng the Gardens into a magical after-dark outdoor art experience. Visitors 
 will journey along an enchanting 800-metre route featuring 11 larger-than-
 life illuminated animal sculptures inspired by Queensland's native wildlif
 e. Designed by Ample Projects in collaboration with First Nations artists 
 Casey Coolwell-Fisher and Nathan Peckham\, Botanic By Night: NightGlow com
 bines art\, storytelling and sound to celebrate the animals\, habitats and
  stories that shape Queensland's natural environment. From kangaroos and k
 oalas to platypus\, dingoes and green tree frogs\, each artwork offers a u
 nique encounter\, inviting visitors to wander\, explore and connect with n
 ature in a whole new way. Perfect for families\, friends and date nights\,
  Botanic By Night: NightGlow also features a dedicated food truck precinct
 .
LOCATION:Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha\, Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt
  Coot-tha\, 152 Mt Coot-tha Road\, Toowong
URL:https://botanicbynight.com.au/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-196kilw@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260927T210000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260927T230000
SUMMARY:Teenage Sex and Death at Camp Miasma
DESCRIPTION:Festival screening. New Farm Cinemas. Direct from winning the Q
 ueer Palm at Cannes\, Hannah Einbinder and Gillian Anderson electrify in t
 his equally camp and bloody psychosexual thriller from queer maverick Jane
  Schoenbrun (I Saw the TV Glow). After years of slapdash sequels and wanin
 g fandom\, the Camp Miasma slasher franchise is handed over to an enthusia
 stic young director (Einbinder\, Hacks) for resurrection. But when she vis
 its the original movie’s star (Anderson\, The X-Files)\, a now-reclusive
  actress shrouded in mystery\, the two women fall into a blood-soaked worl
 d of desire\, fear\, and delirium.
LOCATION:New Farm Cinemas\, 701 Brunswick St\, New Farm
URL:https://www.fivestarcinemas.com.au/new-farm/movie/teenage-sex-and-death
 -at-camp-miasma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1jb65fu@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Stories You Wear: Magpie Goose
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating Country and Culture through the bold designs of Mag
 pie Goose. Museum of Brisbane is excited to collaborate with Magpie Goose\
 , a proudly Aboriginal owned and led fashion and social enterprise\, to ce
 lebrate extraordinary First Nations cultural stories and designs. This exc
 lusive to Brisbane exhibition\, developed in close collaboration with Magp
 ie Goose owners Amanda Hayman (Wakka Wakka and Kalkadoon) and Troy Casey (
 Kamilaroi)\, offers a deep dive into the work of some of the region’s mo
 st talented First Nations artists and designers. Using clothing as a canva
 s for storytelling\, this exciting collaboration will connect audiences wi
 th the rich and diverse cultural expressions of First Nations communities 
 in Queensland and beyond. Discover the artists and stories behind the bran
 d that’s making a difference\, one garment at a time. Stories You Wear: 
 Magpie Goose is supported by the Queensland Government through Arts Queens
 land. Museum of Brisbane is Brisbane City Council’s leading history and 
 art museum where you can experience our city’s vibrant culture. For more
  information\, visit MoB website. Image: Magpie Goose x Quandamooka Artist
 s\, by Amanda Hayman & Troy Casey\, Country to Couture\, 2025\, Photo by D
 ylan Buckee.
LOCATION:Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane City\, Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane
  City Hall\, 64 Adelaide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.museumofbrisbane.com.au/whats-on/stories-you-wear/
END:VEVENT
