BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-atpz0g@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260929T170000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260929T190000
SUMMARY:English linked sword dance
DESCRIPTION:Step into the rhythm of steel and tradition with English Linked
  Sword Dance. This striking folk dance brings together precision\, teamwor
 k\, and centuries of English heritage. Dancers move in tight formations\, 
 each holding a sword linked to the next\, creating intricate patterns\, lo
 cks\, and woven figures that flow seamlessly with the music. The highlight
  comes when the swords are joined to form a star or “lock\,” lifted hi
 gh in a dramatic display of skill and unity. Energetic\, powerful\, and de
 eply communal\, English linked sword dance is as much about cooperation as
  it is about spectacle. No solo stars here - every movement depends on tru
 st\, timing\, and connection with the whole team. Whether you’re drawn b
 y history\, live music\, or the thrill of learning something bold and diff
 erent\, this is your chance to be part of a living tradition. Join us\, ta
 ke a sword\, and become one of the links.
LOCATION:Moorooka Community Centre\, Moorooka\, Moorooka Community Centre\,
  40 Gainsborough Street\, Moorooka
URL:https://www.trumba.com/calendars/brisbane-city-council?eventid=19605508
 5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1mbjk0t@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260929T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260929T200000
SUMMARY:Fallen Angels (1995)
DESCRIPTION:Classic screening. New Farm Cinemas: Fri 25 September Lost soul
 s reach out for human connection amidst the glimmering night world of Hong
  Kong in Wong Kar Wai’s hallucinatory\, neon-soaked nocturne. This hyper
 -cool head rush plays like the dark\, moody flip side to Wong’s breakout
  feature 'Chungking Express' as it charts the subtly interlacing fates of 
 a handful of urban loners\, including a coolly detached hitman (Leon Lai) 
 looking to go straight\, his business partner (Michelle Reis) who secretly
  yearns for him\, and a mute delinquent (Takeshi Kaneshiro) who wreaks mis
 chief by night. Swinging between hardboiled noir and slapstick lunacy with
  giddy abandon\, Fallen Angels is both a dizzying\, dazzling city symphony
  and a poignant meditation on love\, loss\, and longing in a metropolis th
 at never sleeps.
LOCATION:New Farm Cinemas\, 701 Brunswick St\, New Farm
URL:https://www.fivestarcinemas.com.au/new-farm/movie/fallen-angels
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
