UID:brisbane-1wrnyqx@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T170000
SUMMARY:Warrajamba
DESCRIPTION:Follow the mermaid in the bay. Dive into story\, culture and ha
 nds-on creativity with our latest Artist in Residence\, Quandamooka artist
  Delvene Cockatoo-Collins. Journey alongside Delvene to the shores of Minj
 erribah and discover the ancestral story of Warrajamba\, the mermaid\, a l
 iving cultural legacy that Delvene continues to explore as she searches fo
 r its lost ending. Get hands-on and create your own mermaid or dugong usin
 g artist-designed stamps\, connecting with the stories of Warrajamba and Y
 ungong\, the dugong. Discover Delvene’s powerful sculptural work made fr
 om materials gathered from Country - yungair/yungaire (freshwater reed)\, 
 talwalpin (beach hibiscus cotton tree)\, and quampie shell. Come and be im
 mersed in a space that celebrates care for land\, sea and story. MoB’s A
 rtist in Residence program is supported by Tim Fairfax AC. The Creative Sp
 ace is proudly supported by Major Partner Brisbane Airport and generously 
 supported by Ian and Cass George\, and Holly and John Livingstone. Warraja
 mba is supported by the Queensland Government through Arts Queensland. Mus
 eum of Brisbane is Brisbane City Council’s leading history and art museu
 m where you can experience our city’s vibrant culture.
LOCATION:Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane City\, Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane
  City Hall\, 64 Adelaide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.museumofbrisbane.com.au/whats-on/warrajamba/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-w1n13k@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T120000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260930T130000
SUMMARY:Gathering: Muralappi Arts: Jessica Skeen
DESCRIPTION:Gathering presents Muralappi Arts: Jessica Skeen. Jessica Skeen
  is a contemporary Aboriginal artist and founder of Muralappi Arts\, an In
 digenous family-owned business with a proud legacy spanning four generatio
 ns. A Biri and Kuku Thaypan woman from North Queensland\, Jessica was rais
 ed in Logan and continues to live and work there today. Her artistic pract
 ice is grounded in culture\, storytelling\, and connection to Country\, wi
 th works that explore themes of healing\, identity\, and community. Throug
 h murals\, canvas artworks\, and functional art pieces\, Jessica creates p
 owerful visual narratives that foster reflection\, understanding\, and con
 nection. Her work has been featured in hospitals\, public spaces\, and com
 munity initiatives throughout Queensland\, enriching shared spaces with st
 ories that celebrate Aboriginal culture and lived experience. Dedicated to
  sharing culture and knowledge\, Jessica also delivers engaging\, hands-on
  workshops that inspire creativity while promoting cultural understanding 
 and respect. Join us on Wednesday 30 September\, from 12 noon to 1pm\, at 
 the Queen Street Mall Main Stage for a special Muralappi Arts display and 
 showcase presented by Jessica Skeen. This Gathering event is produced by C
 re8tive Nations.
LOCATION:Queen Street Mall\, Brisbane City\, Queen Street Mall\, Queen Stre
 et\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.trumba.com/calendars/LIVE?eventid=205575135
END:VEVENT
