UID:brisbane-1otahvs@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T220000
SUMMARY:Botanic By Night: NightGlow
DESCRIPTION:Botanic By Night: NightGlow makes its Brisbane debut at Brisban
 e Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha from 25 September to 10 October\, transformi
 ng the Gardens into a magical after-dark outdoor art experience. Visitors 
 will journey along an enchanting 800-metre route featuring 11 larger-than-
 life illuminated animal sculptures inspired by Queensland's native wildlif
 e. Designed by Ample Projects in collaboration with First Nations artists 
 Casey Coolwell-Fisher and Nathan Peckham\, Botanic By Night: NightGlow com
 bines art\, storytelling and sound to celebrate the animals\, habitats and
  stories that shape Queensland's natural environment. From kangaroos and k
 oalas to platypus\, dingoes and green tree frogs\, each artwork offers a u
 nique encounter\, inviting visitors to wander\, explore and connect with n
 ature in a whole new way. Perfect for families\, friends and date nights\,
  Botanic By Night: NightGlow also features a dedicated food truck precinct
 .
LOCATION:Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha\, Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt
  Coot-tha\, 152 Mt Coot-tha Road\, Toowong
URL:https://botanicbynight.com.au/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-uebcoe@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T210000
SUMMARY:Angelika Book Club - Verity
DESCRIPTION:Join fellow readers for a special Book Club Screening of Verity
  \, based on the bestselling novel by Colleen Hoover\, on Friday\, October
  2 at 7pm . Adapted from Colleen Hoover's best-selling novel\, this seduct
 ive\, psychological thriller follows renowned author Verity Crawford (Anne
  Hathaway) and Lowen Ashleigh (Dakota Johnson)\, a struggling writer who r
 elocates to the remote Crawford estate to ghostwrite for Verity. After Low
 en uncovers what appears to be Verity's chilling autobiographical notes\, 
 she wrestles with the disturbing and twisted confessions about Verity’s 
 husband Jeremy (Josh Hartnett)\, and finds it hard to separate fiction fro
 m reality\, manipulation from attraction\, and opportunity from obsession.
LOCATION:Angelika Film Centre South City Square\, Woolloongabba
URL:https://angelikacinemas.com.au/movies/details/10478
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-twmzlj@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T210000
SUMMARY:35mm: Pumpkinhead (1988)
DESCRIPTION:35mm Film · Classic screening. New Farm Cinemas. 35mm screenin
 g: Fri 2 October. When a group of teenagers inadvertently kill his only so
 n\, Ed Harley seeks the powers of a backwoods witch to bring the child bac
 k to life. About 35mm: In a world of digital projection and shrinking form
 ats\, celluloid is becoming rare — and we think that matters. We hunt do
 wn original 35mm prints — often unseen for years — and put them back w
 here they belong: on the big screen. This is cinema with depth\, texture\,
  and impact. The way it was meant to be experienced.
LOCATION:New Farm Cinemas\, 701 Brunswick St\, New Farm
URL:https://www.fivestarcinemas.com.au/new-farm/movie/35mm-pumpkinhead
END:VEVENT
