SUMMARY:Crosby Road bushcare
DESCRIPTION:Help regenerate a precious patch of urban bush below Bartley’
 s Hill Lookout in Ascot. We plant native species to attract birds\, bees\,
  bats and lizards\, while removing the invasive plants that crowd them. Jo
 in any monthly working bee starting at 7am on the first Saturday of every 
 month except January. Requirements: Wear protective clothing\, a hat and g
 loves. Insect repellent recommended in summer. No experience necessary. Me
 eting point: We meet near bus stop 21 Bushview on the north side of Crosby
  Road - look for the container with a bat and butterfly mural.
LOCATION:Crosby Road Park\, Ascot\, Crosby Road Park\, 150 Crosby Road\, As
 cot
URL:https://www.trumba.com/calendars/brisbane-city-council?eventid=20643028
 3
