BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1r0pgwc@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T093000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T113000
SUMMARY:Guided walk of the Billai Dhagun Circuit
DESCRIPTION:Join experienced Volunteer Guides in a guided walk through the 
 stunning Boondall Wetlands Reserve. Learn about the unique plants and anim
 als of the wetlands on this gentle\, easy\, all abilities 2km walk. Partic
 ipants can visit the Bird Hide\, observe distinct changes in vegetation\, 
 and discover why Boondall Wetlands is an internationally important conserv
 ation area. Requirements: all children must be accompanied by an adult wea
 r a wide-brimmed hat\, secure and fully enclosed walking shoes\, sun-smart
  clothing\, sunscreen\, and insect repellent bring drinking water and a sn
 ack or picnic lunch as there are no food outlets on site arrive 10minutes 
 early. Note: Walks are subject to weather and environmental conditions.
LOCATION:Boondall Wetlands Environment Centre\, Boondall Wetlands Environme
 nt Centre\, 31 Paperbark Drive (entry via Stanworth Rd)\, Boondall
URL:https://www.trumba.com/calendars/brisbane-city-council?eventid=20635444
 1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-13c7x73@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T170000
SUMMARY:Artist in Residence: Renee Kire
DESCRIPTION:Step inside an exciting new residency project that invites you 
 to experience art in unexpected ways. Artist in Residence Renee Kire takes
  over Museum of Brisbane’s entryway\, transforming these spaces with a v
 ibrant and dynamic mix of striking vinyl graphics and sculptural timber el
 ements. These features create an immersive pathway that stretches across w
 alls and ceilings\, guiding you into the heart of the Museum. Drawing insp
 iration from Minimalism while reinterpreting the movement through a contem
 porary feminist lens\, Kire brings fresh attention to the often-overlooked
  contributions of women in the field. Bright\, colourful and welcoming for
  all visitors\, the artwork is both joyful and thought-provoking. Respondi
 ng directly to the architecture of the Museum\, City Hall and the Brisbane
  cityscape\, Kire’s design reveals unexpected connections between the bu
 ilt environment and abstract form. Repetition\, rhythm and thoughtful deta
 ils invite you to slow down\, look closely and discover new perspectives. 
 MoB’s Artist in Residence program is supported by Tim Fairfax AC. Museum
  of Brisbane is Brisbane City Council’s leading history and art museum w
 here you can experience our city’s vibrant culture.
LOCATION:Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane City\, Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane
  City Hall\, 64 Adelaide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.museumofbrisbane.com.au/whats-on/renee-kire/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-th0h1g@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T170000
SUMMARY:Lord Mayor’s Photographic Awards 2026
DESCRIPTION:Brisbane through the lens of local photographers. The winners e
 xhibition of the 2026 Lord Mayor’s Photographic Awards brings together s
 triking photographic works that capture the city’s spirit - from familia
 r streets and riverside scenes to the fleeting moments\, routines and char
 acters that make Brisbane feel like home. New this year\, the Brisbane Pos
 tcards Collection category invites photographers to showcase Brisbane’s 
 charm and energy through images that locals recognise\, and visitors insta
 ntly fall in love with. Selected winning works will be available as collec
 tible postcards at MoB Shop. Open to anyone who lives\, works or studies i
 n Brisbane\, the 2026 Awards celebrate what makes our city unique through 
 this year’s theme\, Everyday Brisbane. For more information\, visit our 
 website . Museum of Brisbane is Brisbane City Council’s leading history 
 and art museum where you can experience our city’s vibrant culture. For 
 more information\, please visit MoB website .
LOCATION:Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane City\, Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane
  City Hall\, 64 Adelaide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.brisbane.qld.gov.au/events-arts-and-culture/creative-progra
 ms-and-awards/lord-mayor-s-photographic-awards
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-ap1e2h@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T170000
SUMMARY:Warrajamba
DESCRIPTION:Follow the mermaid in the bay. Dive into story\, culture and ha
 nds-on creativity with our latest Artist in Residence\, Quandamooka artist
  Delvene Cockatoo-Collins. Journey alongside Delvene to the shores of Minj
 erribah and discover the ancestral story of Warrajamba\, the mermaid\, a l
 iving cultural legacy that Delvene continues to explore as she searches fo
 r its lost ending. Get hands-on and create your own mermaid or dugong usin
 g artist-designed stamps\, connecting with the stories of Warrajamba and Y
 ungong\, the dugong. Discover Delvene’s powerful sculptural work made fr
 om materials gathered from Country - yungair/yungaire (freshwater reed)\, 
 talwalpin (beach hibiscus cotton tree)\, and quampie shell. Come and be im
 mersed in a space that celebrates care for land\, sea and story. MoB’s A
 rtist in Residence program is supported by Tim Fairfax AC. The Creative Sp
 ace is proudly supported by Major Partner Brisbane Airport and generously 
 supported by Ian and Cass George\, and Holly and John Livingstone. Warraja
 mba is supported by the Queensland Government through Arts Queensland. Mus
 eum of Brisbane is Brisbane City Council’s leading history and art museu
 m where you can experience our city’s vibrant culture.
LOCATION:Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane City\, Museum of Brisbane\, Brisbane
  City Hall\, 64 Adelaide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.museumofbrisbane.com.au/whats-on/warrajamba/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-oalun7@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T123000
SUMMARY:Brisbane Greeters - Greeter's Choice guided walk
DESCRIPTION:Join one of our welcoming and experienced Brisbane Greeters as 
 they share their knowledge and passion for Brisbane on this guided walking
  tour. Explore our booking site to discover a Brisbane Greeters walk to su
 it you\, whether it be in the CBD or one of our most historically signific
 ant suburbs. For locals and visitors alike.
LOCATION:Brisbane City Hall\, Brisbane City\, Brisbane City Hall\, 64 Adela
 ide Street\, Brisbane City
URL:https://www.brisbane.qld.gov.au/events-arts-and-culture/art-and-culture
 /brisbane-greeters-tours
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-9mpiv9@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T120000
SUMMARY:Justene Williams: Once We Were Mudskippers
DESCRIPTION:Spanning performative videos\, sculpture\, sound and installati
 on from the past 20 years\, including a wealth of new works\, ‘Once We W
 ere Mudskippers’ emphasises the aesthetic ambition of Justene Williams
 ’s expansive practice. Like the amphibious fish invoked by the exhibitio
 n’s title\, which exist between worlds\, Williams’s artworks are an am
 algam of materials and approaches and remain grounded in art history while
  reflecting contemporary issues. Adopting a do-it-yourself strategy\, Will
 iams fuses disparate textures and concepts into compelling artworks that s
 peak to her belief that our shared future can be forged with resources at 
 hand and transformed by the imagination. Williams’s artworks address ide
 als of beauty\, careerist and consumerist pressures\, the strangeness of l
 iving in both the physical body and virtual space\, and human connections 
 to rituals and the afterlife. ‘Once We Were Mudskippers’ is characteri
 sed by Justene Williams’s unwavering conviction that art is a world wher
 e artists and audiences can experiment and commune.
LOCATION:QAG\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/exhibition/justene-williams-once-we-were-
 mudskippers
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
