UID:brisbane-1jb8ssm@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261004T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261004T220000
SUMMARY:Botanic By Night: NightGlow
DESCRIPTION:Botanic By Night: NightGlow makes its Brisbane debut at Brisban
 e Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha from 25 September to 10 October\, transformi
 ng the Gardens into a magical after-dark outdoor art experience. Visitors 
 will journey along an enchanting 800-metre route featuring 11 larger-than-
 life illuminated animal sculptures inspired by Queensland's native wildlif
 e. Designed by Ample Projects in collaboration with First Nations artists 
 Casey Coolwell-Fisher and Nathan Peckham\, Botanic By Night: NightGlow com
 bines art\, storytelling and sound to celebrate the animals\, habitats and
  stories that shape Queensland's natural environment. From kangaroos and k
 oalas to platypus\, dingoes and green tree frogs\, each artwork offers a u
 nique encounter\, inviting visitors to wander\, explore and connect with n
 ature in a whole new way. Perfect for families\, friends and date nights\,
  Botanic By Night: NightGlow also features a dedicated food truck precinct
 .
LOCATION:Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha\, Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt
  Coot-tha\, 152 Mt Coot-tha Road\, Toowong
URL:https://botanicbynight.com.au/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-8irb4@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20230920T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20230920T120000
SUMMARY:Small Figures
DESCRIPTION:The Collection Online team have been busy photographing thousan
 ds of artworks as part of QAGOMA’s Digital Transformation Initiative. Th
 is makes the Collection available and accessible to people everywhere\, in
  detail never seen before. With dedicated conservators\, registrars\, tech
 nologists and photographers\, the project has provided the resources to de
 lve deep into Collection Storage to uncover and care for artworks not disp
 layed in decades. This exhibition represents a small sample of our teams
 ’ favourite finds – the weird and whimsical\, the cute and curious. We
  gratefully acknowledge the hundreds of donors who generously supported th
 e QAGOMA Foundation’s ‘Unlock the Collection’ campaign to digitise t
 he Collection and make artworks more accessible and discoverable online in
 cluding this diverse range of artworks\, from small figures to small frogs
 . These are some of the artworks we have recently prepared for photography
 \, and just some of the works which made us smile.
LOCATION:QAG\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/exhibition/small-figures
END:VEVENT
