UID:brisbane-zv1hxq@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T153000
SUMMARY:Audrey Gibbs Art Prize
DESCRIPTION:Audrey Gibbs joined the Royal Queensland Art Society in 1983 an
 d was recognised as a Fellow of the society in 2009. This exhibition explo
 res genre artworks\, one of Audrey’s great pleasures. This exhibition fo
 cuses on Genre Artworks\, one of Audrey's favourite themes to paint. Genre
  Artworks are those that depict ordinary people in everyday situations\, b
 oth in the exterior and the interior. Rather than heroic or mythological s
 ubjects\, these works celebrate the familiar: everyday people participatin
 g in domestic routines\, work\, leisure\, social gatherings\, and quiet mo
 ments of daily life. The Royal Queensland Art Society is proudly supported
  by Brisbane City Council.
LOCATION:Petrie Terrace Gallery\, Petrie Terrace\, Petrie Terrace Gallery\,
  162 Petrie Terrace\, Petrie Terrace
URL:https://rqas.com.au/event/audrey-gibbs-art-prize/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-qqmv4r@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T103000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T111500
SUMMARY:Meet Wildlife Neighbours (6 + years)
DESCRIPTION:Brisbane is Australia’s most biodiverse capital city. Native 
 wildlife live all around us — from our backyards to local parks and natu
 re reserves. But have you ever met these unique animals face to face? Join
  our wildlife expert for an engaging and immersive session in nature\, whe
 re you'll meet your wild neighbours and some of Brisbane's most iconic ani
 mals. Discover what makes them special\, how they live\, and the vital rol
 e they play in our ecosystems. Your actions matter. By learning more about
  our native species\, you’ll be empowered to make simple changes — lik
 e planting native vegetation or keeping pets indoors at night. These actio
 ns help protect our incredible biodiversity and ensure our wildlife neighb
 ours continue to thrive. Requirements on the day: Arrive minimum 10 minute
 s early to check in with staff at the centre. All children must be accompa
 nied and directly supervised by an adult. Wear a hat\, sun-safe clothing\,
  fully enclosed shoes\, sunscreen\, and bring insect repellent as some sho
 ws may take place outside. Bring water and a snack if required\, as there 
 are no food outlets on site. Note: Events are subject to weather and envir
 onmental conditions and may be cancelled on the day.
LOCATION:Downfall Creek Bushland Centre\, Downfall Creek Bushland Centre\, 
 815 Rode Road\, Chermside West
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com.au/e/meet-wildlife-neighbours-6-years-ticket
 s-1997952286071?aff=oddtdtcreator
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1tot7uk@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261002T130000
SUMMARY:The Two Tenors featuring The Best of Josh Groban
DESCRIPTION:World-Class Voices. One Unforgettable Show. Following the succe
 ss of Timeless Duets\, a sold-out season of The Two Tenors – The Best of
  Josh Groban at Wynnum Fringe Festival\, and a performance to more than 1\
 ,600 people at the prestigious Lord Mayor's City Hall Concerts\, Vavachi E
 ntertainment is delighted to return to Sandgate Town Hall with its excitin
 g new production\, The Two Tenors – The Best of Josh Groban. As part of 
 Queensland Seniors Month\, we would love to invite your members to enjoy t
 his uplifting morning of world-class entertainment. Starring former The Te
 n Tenors member Roger Davy\, Gold Palm Award-winning musical theatre perfo
 rmer Matthew Leigh\, and special guest soprano Gabrielle Diaz from Opera Q
 ueensland and The 7 Sopranos\, this inspiring concert celebrates the timel
 ess music of Josh Groban alongside much-loved classical crossover favourit
 es. Audiences will enjoy songs including You Raise Me Up\, The Prayer\, To
  Where You Are\, Bridge Over Troubled Water\, Time to Say Goodbye\, and ma
 ny more\, together with a wonderful selection of Broadway favourites\, lig
 ht opera and contemporary classics. Together\, these three exceptional art
 ists deliver an elegant and uplifting concert experience filled with warmt
 h\, humour and breathtaking vocal brilliance. Three Voices. One Extraordin
 ary Morning. Pure Vocal Brilliance.
LOCATION:Sandgate Town Hall\, Sandgate\, Sandgate Town Hall\, corner of Cli
 ff and Seymour Streets\, Sandgate
URL:https://www.trybooking.com/DNSGP
END:VEVENT
