BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-15ttobl@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261001T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261001T140000
SUMMARY:School holiday activity - Spring hub - Flower power
DESCRIPTION:Discover the fascinating world of flowers and the peculiar Poll
 inators who work with them at our Spring hub school holiday activities at 
 the Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha. Take off on a scientific explora
 tion of our Sensory Garden\, bursting with blooms of all shapes and sizes 
 and bring your findings back to the hub where you can take a closer look w
 ith microscopes and magnifying glasses. Get your hands dirty and turn scie
 nce into art by making 3D clay pollen models and sensational seed balls. F
 inally compile all your field notes and decorate them with pen or a paintb
 rush while you discover more about the precious pollinators who help to ke
 ep our flowers fantastic and our fruit plentiful. Bring a picnic blanket a
 nd lunch to enjoy on our grassy lawn. Note: Children under 16 are to be ac
 companied by an adult. Location : Meet at the Auditorium lawn. Please wear
  a hat and enclosed shoes\; and bring a keep cup or water bottle. This wor
 kshop supports the Botanic Gardens' commitment to creating a plant loving 
 community dedicated to putting the plant back into planet. For more inform
 ation\, send an email .
LOCATION:Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt Coot-tha\, Brisbane Botanic Gardens Mt
